    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "09d05831_48e08147",
        "filename": "drivers/virt/halla/hvm_mmu.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 218,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-28T09:58:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the flow is:\n\n * `hvm_insert_ppage()` returns `-EEXIST` and so `pin_one_page()` drops the pin, sets `*out_page \u003d page` and returns 0\n * `hvm_vm_allocate_guest_page()` then returns 0 and sets `*pfn` to the pfn for the _unpinned_ page\n * `hvm_map_guest()` is then called with this pfn and passes it to the `HVC_FID_HVM_MAP_GUEST` hypercall\n \nWhy do you think the hypercall is not invoked in this case?",
      "parentUuid": "acd52876_85b7f96e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 218,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 218,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "80fd139bccee9642014f4f85afc86fbbfd397096",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "210bbbff_ac2730b4",
        "filename": "drivers/virt/halla/hvm_mmu.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 218,
      "author": {
        "id": 1667998
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-28T10:22:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I missed last code of pin_one_page..:( \nThe same pfn will enter hypercall in each vcpu. And Hypervisor handles the same pfn.\nThen, isn\u0027t there a pinning problem?",
      "parentUuid": "09d05831_48e08147",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 218,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 218,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "80fd139bccee9642014f4f85afc86fbbfd397096",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "26bc4a89_ca71af2a",
        "filename": "drivers/virt/halla/hvm_mmu.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 218,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-28T11:11:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Couldn\u0027t crosvm change its mapping (e.g. by calling `mmap()`) in between the two pin operations and you would get a different pfn?\n\nI think the best approach is:\n\n1. Return `-EAGAIN` after unpinning the page if `hyp_insert_ppage()` returned `-EEXIST`\n2. Return 0 immediately from `handle_demand_page()` if `hvm_vm_allocate_guest_page()` returns `-EAGAIN`\n\nIt\u0027s also critical that the `HVC_FID_HVM_MAP_GUEST` hypercall does not allow the host to replace an existing stage-2 mapping with another one for a different address.",
      "parentUuid": "210bbbff_ac2730b4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 218,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 218,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "80fd139bccee9642014f4f85afc86fbbfd397096",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
